        "Newton's Second Law establishes the mathematical relationship between force, mass, momentum, and acceleration.",
        "Newton's Third Law states that every action force has an equal and opposite reaction force.",
        "The Law of Conservation of Momentum governs system interactions when no external force acts.",
        "Friction acts as a resistive contact force possessing both essential advantages and energy-loss disadvantages."
      ],
