    {
      "id": "jkm1qbu",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "TYPES OF FORCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "4r316vf",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "Contact Force – Requires physical contact Example: Friction, Muscular force",
        "Non-Contact Force – Acts from a distance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hav7tra",
      "content": "Example: Gravitational force, Magnetic force, Electrostatic force"
    },
    {
      "id": "f1f1udm",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "NEWTON’S FIRST LAW OF MOTION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7asq9mm",
      "content": "Statement:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jfz3j6z",
      "content": "An object remains at rest or in uniform motion in a straight line unless acted upon by an external force."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ldpcivx",
      "content": "This law is also known as the Law of Inertia. Inertia:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3incc1d",
      "content": "The tendency of an object to resist change in its state of motion."
    },
    {
      "id": "opt6p4t",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Types of Inertia"
    },
    {
      "id": "p52hkgk",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "Inertia of Rest",
        "Inertia of Motion",
        "Inertia of Direction"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "xinfdw0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "NEWTON’S SECOND LAW OF MOTION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "eok2ukm",
      "content": "Statement:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vl0zi71",
      "content": "The rate of change of momentum of an object is directly proportional to the applied force and takes place in the direction of force."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "s9w1bvr",
      "content": "Formula:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jptxpkq",
      "content": "Force = Mass × Acceleration F = ma"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6sthcmd",
      "content": "SI Unit of Force = Newton"
    },
    {
      "id": "jtejfv2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "MOMENTUM"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "i1k2bnz",
      "content": "Momentum is the product of mass and velocity. Formula:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "retuu5k",
      "content": "Momentum = Mass × Velocity p = mv"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "1qyn3fh",
      "content": "Unit: kg m/s"
    },
    {
      "id": "l67kevc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "NEWTON’S THIRD LAW OF MOTION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ot4z5pr",
      "content": "Statement:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0psn4u2",
      "content": "For every action, there is an equal and opposite reaction."
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Feature",
        "Advantages of Friction",
        "Disadvantages of Friction"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Motion Control",
          "Enables safe walking, running, driving, and braking",
          "Opposes motion, requiring additional energy to maintain speed"
        ],
        [
          "Material Impact",
          "Prevents slipping and provides necessary grip",
          "Causes continuous wear and tear of machine parts and footwear"
        ],
        [
          "Energy Outcome",
          "Facilitates power transmission through belts and pulleys",
          "Converts useful kinetic energy into wasted thermal energy"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "y76cytx"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cgvzxtg",
      "content": "Examples:"
    },
    {
      "id": "2my6up7",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Walking</li><li>Swimming</li><li>Recoil of gun</li></ul>",
        "Walking",
        "Swimming",
        "Recoil of gun"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "86ttuht",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "LAW OF CONSERVATION OF MOMENTUM"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "k6xsbff",
      "content": "According to this law, the total momentum of a system remains constant if no external force acts on it."
    },
    {
      "id": "vn2325p",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "FRICTION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9igj7tt",
      "content": "Friction is the force that opposes motion between two surfaces in contact. Types of Friction:"
    },
    {
      "id": "2yp7b4e",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "Static friction",
        "Sliding friction",
        "Rolling friction"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ll4bwfa",
      "content": "Rolling friction is the least."
    },
    {
      "id": "x29vje5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "ADVANTAGES AND DISADVANTAGES OF FRICTION"
